# Purpose

The Apple TV Module enables Aura to interact with Apple TV as naturally as any Apple application while respecting Apple's platform limitations.

Aura should never attempt to replace tvOS.

Instead, Aura complements the Apple TV experience.

---

# Current Public API Gate

`ADR/ADR-007-apple-tv-public-capability-scope.md` records the public capability assessment. `ADR/ADR-009-personal-apple-tv-protocol-experiment.md` authorizes a narrowly scoped undocumented LAN protocol implementation for the owner's private TestFlight or direct-Xcode build.

The remainder of this document records the desired product experience. It is not evidence that Apple provides a public API for those capabilities.

The current assessment found no public iPhone API for a third-party app to pair with and directly control Apple TV system navigation, power, playback, Now Playing state or applications.

The proposal to omit direct Apple TV control was rejected. Apple TV remains a Version 1 requirement. ADR-009 explicitly accepts an experimental reverse-engineered network protocol for single-owner distribution while continuing to prohibit Apple private framework calls.

During the experiment:

• Protocol code must remain isolated inside the Apple TV integration boundary
• Pairing credentials must be stored only in Keychain
• Direct commands may ship only after real-hardware verification
• Unsupported controls must remain absent from production UI
• Mock Apple TV data is preview-only and does not prove capability support

Public system-mediated routes are limited to:

• Apple's Control Center Remote, presented as external user guidance rather than Aura control
• AirPlay route selection for media Aura itself owns
• Aggregate HomeKit home-hub state and runtime HomeKit characteristics actually exposed
• User-composed Shortcuts that combine system actions with future Aura App Intents
• A future same-team Aura tvOS companion through a separately approved Handoff design

